  "scenario": "An e-commerce class model mistakenly uses Generalization between OrderItem and Order (an OrderItem is not a type of Order!). Instead, an Order strictly owns its OrderItems, Customer places Orders, and OrderItem references a Product.",
  "goal": "Fix the invalid inheritance edge and model the true ownership and association relationships.",
  "learningObjective": "Correctly replace mistaken inheritance ('is-a') with Composition ('owns-a') and Associations.",
  "hints": [
    "Check the relationship between OrderItem and Order — Composition should replace Generalization.",
    "Make sure the Composition arrow starts at the owner (Order -> OrderItem).",
    "Keep Customer -> Order and OrderItem -> Product as Associations."
  ],
  "solutionExplanation": "Order composes OrderItem (strict ownership), while Customer associates with Order and OrderItem associates with Product.",
